# Provider binaries and local backend scratch. 117 MB of downloaded plugin, and
# `terraform init` regenerates all of it.
.terraform/

# State never lives in the tree. It lives in the GCS backend, and a local copy
# committed here would be both a secret leak and a second source of truth that
# CI would fight.
*.tfstate
*.tfstate.*
crash.log
crash.*.log

# Deliberately NOT ignored, and both matter:
#
#   .terraform.lock.hcl   committed, so provider versions are identical between a
#                         workstation and CI. Ignoring it makes a green local run
#                         mean less than it looks.
#
#   *.auto.tfvars         committed, because that is where the web host and mail
#                         provider decisions land. Terraform loads them
#                         automatically, so the decision arrives as a reviewable
#                         file in a pull request rather than as a code change or
#                         as an untracked value someone holds locally.
